## 1. What the Bot is

JarBot Testing is an **experimental, internal testing application** used to develop and test the bots of the [JarBot repository](https://github.com/Jarjarbin-Studio/JarBot), built with [JarDiscordEngine](https://github.com/Jarjarbin-Studio/JarDiscordEngine). It is **not a finished product and not intended for general public use**.

Specifically:

- The Bot's credentials may be used by **several different bot clients and engine builds**, which are run **locally** by the developer (on the developer's own machines or development environments), not as a permanently hosted service.
- Features, commands and behaviour **change constantly** and may break, appear, or disappear at any time.
- It may be offline most of the time and may go on or offline without notice.
- Any stored data may be reset or deleted at any time.

We recommend adding the Bot **only to servers dedicated to testing**, and only if you know and trust the developer.

## 2. Scope of use: everything Discord allows

For testing purposes, the Bot is deliberately **not limited to a specific feature set**. It may use any capability that Discord makes available to bots, within the rules set by Discord, including:

- **All Gateway Intents**, including the privileged ones (Server Members, Presence, and Message Content);
- **Any permission** a server administrator grants it, up to and including Administrator;
- **Any scope** you authorize, including `bot`, `applications.commands`, and, where you choose to authorize them, OAuth2 scopes such as `identify`, `email`, `guilds`, `guilds.members.read` and `connections`;
- reading, sending, editing and deleting messages, embeds, attachments, reactions, polls, threads, and forum posts;
- slash commands, context-menu commands, buttons, select menus, modals and other interactions;
- managing roles, channels, emojis, stickers, scheduled events, webhooks, invites, auto-moderation rules and other server settings;
- moderation actions (timeouts, kicks, bans);
- joining voice and stage channels, and voice features;
- direct messages with users.

**Granting permissions is your choice.** The Bot can only do what Discord and the server's administrators allow. If you do not want the Bot to have a given capability, do not grant it, or do not add the Bot to your server. You can remove the Bot, or revoke its permissions and OAuth2 authorizations, at any time.

